1
00:00:00,012 --> 00:00:01,888
[bawling]

2
00:00:04,015 --> 00:00:10,022
My chocolate, my games, Momohiki!
Where are you?

3
00:00:10,105 --> 00:00:10,939
Huh?

4
00:00:11,023 --> 00:00:11,940
[gasps]

5
00:00:14,818 --> 00:00:17,446
Momohiki!

6
00:00:18,113 --> 00:00:20,991
I missed you so much!

7
00:00:21,074 --> 00:00:23,910
[smooching]

8
00:00:23,994 --> 00:00:26,538
Hey, you feel kinda buff.

9
00:00:26,621 --> 00:00:28,874
What happened? Hmm?

10
00:00:28,957 --> 00:00:32,294
[Momohiki] Anzu, dear, I saw you
having lots of fun with that hottie.

11
00:00:32,961 --> 00:00:35,338
[shrieks, screams]

12
00:00:36,923 --> 00:00:40,051
I was thrown around by the plane,
and then thrown around in Times Square.

13
00:00:40,135 --> 00:00:41,386
It's been rough for me.

14
00:00:43,013 --> 00:00:44,514
What happened, Momohiki?

15
00:00:44,598 --> 00:00:46,808
You've transformed.
You're just like a person

16
00:00:46,892 --> 00:00:50,020
in those ads that say,
"Weight Training Changed My Life."

17
00:00:52,647 --> 00:00:54,483
[Momohiki] I guess
you don't need me anymore.

18
00:00:55,358 --> 00:00:57,069
-Goodbye to you, Anzu.
-[gasps]

19
00:00:57,152 --> 00:00:59,279
Wait, Momohiki!

20
00:00:59,362 --> 00:01:05,243
It's not like that.

21
00:01:05,327 --> 00:01:08,455
-[meowing]
-[phone buzzing]

22
00:01:08,538 --> 00:01:10,290
[moans]
Momohiki…

23
00:01:10,373 --> 00:01:12,042
[meowing continues]

24
00:01:12,125 --> 00:01:13,126
[buzzing continues]

25
00:01:13,210 --> 00:01:15,295
[Anzu] Hm, it's the alarm.

26
00:01:16,630 --> 00:01:17,798
[Anzu sighs]

27
00:01:17,881 --> 00:01:18,882
Is it morning?

28
00:01:20,383 --> 00:01:21,802
[meowing continues]

29
00:01:25,388 --> 00:01:26,306
[exhales deeply]

30
00:01:29,768 --> 00:01:31,019
-[grunts]
-[gasps]

31
00:01:31,102 --> 00:01:32,229
[groans]

32
00:01:32,312 --> 00:01:33,313
A cat?

33
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:36,983
[shrieks]

34
00:01:37,067 --> 00:01:37,901
[grunts in pain]

35
00:01:38,485 --> 00:01:39,319
[Tsukasa] My tongue…

36
00:01:40,028 --> 00:01:41,238
[screams]

37
00:01:41,321 --> 00:01:42,948
Quiet! You and that alarm!

38
00:01:43,031 --> 00:01:45,408
What… What… Wh-- What…

39
00:01:45,492 --> 00:01:46,827
Just so you know,

40
00:01:47,452 --> 00:01:49,579
you're the one
who made us stay up playing games,

41
00:01:49,663 --> 00:01:51,915
and then you dozed off
and you wouldn't let go of my hand.

42
00:01:52,833 --> 00:01:55,085
Thanks to you,
I was stuck here all night long.

43
00:01:55,836 --> 00:01:58,088
I don't remember.

44
00:01:58,171 --> 00:02:01,758
[Anzu] Wait a sec, was I sleeping
on his lap all night?

45
00:02:01,842 --> 00:02:03,969
Ah, I'm so embarrassed!

46
00:02:04,469 --> 00:02:05,929
Hold on! That's what embarrasses you?

47
00:02:06,012 --> 00:02:08,807
What about walking around
in an outfit like that?

48
00:02:09,975 --> 00:02:12,602
-I'm so sorry. You must have been cold.
-[sighs]

49
00:02:12,686 --> 00:02:14,229
[Tsukasa] My body's hurts.

50
00:02:14,312 --> 00:02:15,397
-Ugh.
-[sighs]

51
00:02:17,065 --> 00:02:20,569
It's nice out now.
I gotta go home and get ready.

52
00:02:21,486 --> 00:02:22,863
[Anzu] Time for serious self-reflection.

53
00:02:22,946 --> 00:02:24,406
REMORSEFUL: TO BE FILLED WITH REMORSE

54
00:02:24,489 --> 00:02:26,908
[approaching footsteps]

55
00:02:28,201 --> 00:02:30,287
So, thanks for letting me stay here.

56
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:33,915
[Anzu] Oh, huh, no worries,
I'm sorry about everything.

57
00:02:35,709 --> 00:02:37,419
-See you.
-Okay.

58
00:02:40,088 --> 00:02:41,047
[door closes]

59
00:02:41,131 --> 00:02:44,467
[Anzu] I meant to set my alarm
to go off way earlier than this.

60
00:02:45,260 --> 00:02:48,430
I wonder if Kazuki
will have enough time to…

61
00:02:48,513 --> 00:02:49,681
Oh, no, shoot!

62
00:02:49,764 --> 00:02:52,684
I can't believe I forgot
to give him his lunch!

63
00:02:52,767 --> 00:02:54,060
[groans]

64
00:02:54,144 --> 00:02:56,313
Guess I have to give it to him at school.

65
00:02:57,564 --> 00:02:58,815
-Here.
-Thanks.

66
00:02:58,899 --> 00:03:00,567
-[chatter]
-[girl 1] Who does she think she is?

67
00:03:00,650 --> 00:03:02,527
[girl 2] She better not think
she can get away with this!

68
00:03:02,611 --> 00:03:03,486
[screams]

69
00:03:04,070 --> 00:03:05,155
[groans]

70
00:03:10,994 --> 00:03:12,996
[theme music]

71
00:04:36,246 --> 00:04:37,122
[door closes]

72
00:04:37,956 --> 00:04:41,167
#3: MY LIFE HAS BECOME A DATING SIM

73
00:04:42,752 --> 00:04:43,962
[sighs]

74
00:04:45,422 --> 00:04:46,256
Mm…

75
00:04:47,299 --> 00:04:48,591
[Anzu] So that means

76
00:04:48,675 --> 00:04:52,178
that I was holding
Kazuki's hand all night long, right?

77
00:04:53,263 --> 00:04:55,849
And I even slept on his lap.

78
00:04:58,184 --> 00:04:59,352
[gasps]

79
00:04:59,853 --> 00:05:03,189
Wait a minute! I can't even remember
what time I dozed off.

80
00:05:03,273 --> 00:05:06,026
I do remember talking to that devil and…

81
00:05:06,109 --> 00:05:07,360
-and that thing was…
-[doorbell rings]

82
00:05:07,444 --> 00:05:09,029
[gasps]
Who is…

83
00:05:09,863 --> 00:05:11,489
What is it? Uh…

84
00:05:12,115 --> 00:05:15,368
-[Anzu] Huh, Kazuki?
-Um…

85
00:05:17,662 --> 00:05:18,997
So, about my place…

86
00:05:22,375 --> 00:05:24,586
Aah… Are you kidding me?

87
00:05:24,669 --> 00:05:27,797
Did it sink in the Tokyo Bay or something?

88
00:05:29,883 --> 00:05:31,801
[comical music]

89
00:05:32,510 --> 00:05:34,888
Maybe there's a weird plumbing issue
or something,

90
00:05:34,971 --> 00:05:36,890
because it seems like
only my unit was flooded.

91
00:05:36,973 --> 00:05:37,807
What?

92
00:05:38,391 --> 00:05:41,019
[Tsukasa] My uniform
and textbooks are all drenched.

93
00:05:41,102 --> 00:05:43,313
Guess I gotta skip school today.

94
00:05:44,230 --> 00:05:46,733
Hey, um, can I borrow your phone?

95
00:05:46,816 --> 00:05:49,027
[Anzu] Oh, huh, sure. Go ahead.

96
00:05:49,110 --> 00:05:50,070
Great. Thanks.

97
00:05:54,741 --> 00:05:58,828
[Anzu] I know exactly who's responsible.
They caused this ridiculous situation.

98
00:05:58,912 --> 00:06:00,455
[Riri] Water blast!

99
00:06:00,538 --> 00:06:02,082
Yes. Thanks a lot.

100
00:06:03,041 --> 00:06:04,209
[Anzu] Gosh dang it!

101
00:06:04,709 --> 00:06:06,711
-Thanks for that.
-Oh, sure.

102
00:06:08,546 --> 00:06:09,380
So, everything's fine…

103
00:06:13,009 --> 00:06:14,803
Never mind. I take that back.

104
00:06:15,929 --> 00:06:17,555
[birds chirping]

105
00:06:18,973 --> 00:06:20,892
Is there anything that I can do to help?

106
00:06:21,935 --> 00:06:24,437
Yeah, why don't you give me
your phone number?

107
00:06:24,521 --> 00:06:26,147
Huh? Sure.

108
00:06:26,231 --> 00:06:28,108
Hmm… Just a sec.

109
00:06:28,191 --> 00:06:29,317
[scribbling]

110
00:06:30,276 --> 00:06:31,111
[Anzu] Here.

111
00:06:31,611 --> 00:06:33,863
[Tsukasa] I'll call you
if anything comes up.

112
00:06:33,947 --> 00:06:35,031
Okay.

113
00:06:36,616 --> 00:06:40,286
-Oh, yeah, you forgot your lunch.
-Oh, thank you.

114
00:06:43,331 --> 00:06:44,874
You packed it really well,

115
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:46,626
but, um…

116
00:06:46,709 --> 00:06:49,420
-[meowing]
-…did you have to use this bag?

117
00:06:49,504 --> 00:06:52,215
[Anzu] Oh, well, it seemed like
the perfect size.

118
00:06:52,298 --> 00:06:53,633
And I couldn't bring you lunch.

119
00:06:54,342 --> 00:06:57,178
All of your fangirls
would think of me as their enemy.

120
00:06:57,262 --> 00:06:58,096
[sighs]

121
00:06:58,179 --> 00:07:00,306
When I'm the one
who really made most of the lunch.

122
00:07:00,390 --> 00:07:01,224
[chuckles]

123
00:07:02,976 --> 00:07:04,644
Well, thank you.

124
00:07:05,478 --> 00:07:07,772
Hoshino, you should get going.

125
00:07:07,856 --> 00:07:10,400
-Oh, ye-- Yeah.
-I gotta go.

126
00:07:10,483 --> 00:07:11,609
You've got this.

127
00:07:16,531 --> 00:07:17,657
[sighs]

128
00:07:20,994 --> 00:07:23,663
[Riri grunting]

129
00:07:26,082 --> 00:07:28,168
[Riri laughing mischievously]

130
00:07:28,251 --> 00:07:30,670
[indistinct chatter]

131
00:07:31,337 --> 00:07:33,173
-Hey!
-[laughs]

132
00:07:33,256 --> 00:07:36,176
[light music]

133
00:07:37,510 --> 00:07:39,679
[yawns]

134
00:07:40,597 --> 00:07:43,183
I'm looking for a room
to move into right away.

135
00:07:43,766 --> 00:07:45,643
[Tsukasa grunts]

136
00:07:47,729 --> 00:07:49,189
[old man grunts]

137
00:07:49,272 --> 00:07:50,190
[Tsukasa] Huh?

138
00:07:51,816 --> 00:07:53,067
Can I help you?

139
00:07:53,151 --> 00:07:54,152
[old man gasps]

140
00:07:55,278 --> 00:07:57,447
[old man grunts]

141
00:07:57,530 --> 00:08:00,200
-[old man] Thank you very much.
-[Tsukasa] No problem.

142
00:08:00,283 --> 00:08:02,827
-[school bell rings]
-[students chattering]

143
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:04,746
[Saki] Hey, Anzu.

144
00:08:06,331 --> 00:08:08,958
-So, you brought your lunch today, huh?
-Yeah.

145
00:08:09,042 --> 00:08:12,045
You made that all by yourself? Awesome.

146
00:08:12,128 --> 00:08:12,962
[laughs awkwardly]

147
00:08:14,422 --> 00:08:16,549
[Anzu] Should I confide in Saki

148
00:08:16,633 --> 00:08:19,886
about the whole
complicated situation with Kazuki?

149
00:08:21,054 --> 00:08:25,225
But I don't wanna drag
my precious friend into this.

150
00:08:25,308 --> 00:08:27,769
BROKEN PHONE, CAN'T GET HOME,
MAJOR FLOODING

151
00:08:27,852 --> 00:08:30,104
-[gasps]
-[phone buzzing]

152
00:08:30,188 --> 00:08:32,148
-An unknown number's calling me?
-Oh?

153
00:08:32,232 --> 00:08:34,943
-Oh, you can eat.
-Okay.

154
00:08:35,026 --> 00:08:36,236
This is Anzu.

155
00:08:36,945 --> 00:08:38,863
[Tsukasa] Your scrambled eggs
are too sweet.

156
00:08:38,947 --> 00:08:40,990
-[gasps]
-It's a damn omelet!

157
00:08:41,074 --> 00:08:42,325
Oops, sorry.

158
00:08:43,409 --> 00:08:45,245
How are you calling?

159
00:08:46,246 --> 00:08:48,081
-Just bought a new phone
-[Anzu] What?

160
00:08:48,581 --> 00:08:51,209
Hey, are you free after school?

161
00:08:51,292 --> 00:08:54,546
[Anzu] Uh, well,
I don't have anything planned.

162
00:08:54,629 --> 00:08:57,757
Then, can you meet me
at Toutor by the station?

163
00:08:58,591 --> 00:08:59,634
Yeah, sure.

164
00:08:59,717 --> 00:09:01,886
-[Tsukasa] All right, see you later.
-[line beeps]

165
00:09:02,554 --> 00:09:05,515
He hung up, jeez. Could have said more.

166
00:09:05,598 --> 00:09:06,766
Your friend?

167
00:09:07,433 --> 00:09:10,186
Uh, yeah… Well, let's eat then.

168
00:09:12,230 --> 00:09:14,148
[Saki] Wow, looks delicious.

169
00:09:14,232 --> 00:09:18,861
Sausages, sauteed spinach,
meat rolls, and scrambled eggs!

170
00:09:18,945 --> 00:09:20,280
It's an omelet roll!

171
00:09:21,114 --> 00:09:21,948
[Anzu] Hmm.

172
00:09:22,031 --> 00:09:25,285
So I guess he did end up
having to buy a new phone after all,

173
00:09:25,994 --> 00:09:30,582
even though he said he's broke.
Jeez, this is all my fault. I feel so bad.

174
00:09:31,916 --> 00:09:34,836
-Wait! This is all that devil's fault!
-[Riri giggling]

175
00:09:35,837 --> 00:09:37,839
-[student 1] All right, see ya!
-[student 2] See ya!

176
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:41,259
-[Rena] Oh, teacher.
-[teacher] Hm?

177
00:09:41,342 --> 00:09:45,179
I heard Tsukasa's house's flooded.
Is everything all right there?

178
00:09:45,263 --> 00:09:48,474
Oh, well, I was just about
to call him and find out.

179
00:09:49,100 --> 00:09:53,396
Oh, but I heard that
Tsukasa's phone was broken.

180
00:09:53,479 --> 00:09:55,315
What? But I think the number

181
00:09:55,398 --> 00:09:57,775
he called from before
belonged to a cell phone.

182
00:09:57,859 --> 00:10:00,820
No way.
I guess he must've bought one then.

183
00:10:00,903 --> 00:10:02,071
All right, give me his number.

184
00:10:02,155 --> 00:10:04,741
-Well, I can't help you with that.
-You're a meanie.

185
00:10:05,325 --> 00:10:08,244
Well, Mister, I would still like
to hear that boy's voice.

186
00:10:08,328 --> 00:10:09,662
So put the speaker on.

187
00:10:09,746 --> 00:10:11,080
Hey! Come on!

188
00:10:11,164 --> 00:10:12,081
CONNECTED

189
00:10:12,165 --> 00:10:14,334
-[Anzu] Yes. Hello?
-What?

190
00:10:15,793 --> 00:10:19,589
Um, yes, hello there.
Have I reached Kazuki's cell phone?

191
00:10:20,256 --> 00:10:23,593
[Anzu] Huh? Kazuki's phone? No, uh…

192
00:10:24,510 --> 00:10:26,095
-No, it's not.
-[teacher] Hm?

193
00:10:26,179 --> 00:10:27,680
-Wait! What?
-Huh?

194
00:10:29,307 --> 00:10:30,183
Wha--

195
00:10:36,314 --> 00:10:38,149
This rent's expensive.

196
00:10:38,691 --> 00:10:41,110
-Hey, don't you think that guy next to us…
-[girl] Hm-mm.

197
00:10:41,194 --> 00:10:43,529
-…is way hot? Should I get his number?
-[Tsukasa] Hm?

198
00:10:45,782 --> 00:10:47,533
[Tsukasa] Man, I should have worn a hat.

199
00:10:49,786 --> 00:10:50,620
Huh?

200
00:10:50,703 --> 00:10:51,746
Uh…

201
00:10:52,705 --> 00:10:53,831
[sighs]

202
00:10:55,750 --> 00:10:57,210
[Tsukasa] She's taking forever.

203
00:11:01,923 --> 00:11:02,799
[gasps]

204
00:11:03,841 --> 00:11:04,926
Uh…

205
00:11:06,219 --> 00:11:07,637
Hey, Tsukasa.

206
00:11:07,720 --> 00:11:08,930
[Tsukasa groans]

207
00:11:09,722 --> 00:11:12,266
I heard all about
what happened to your place.

208
00:11:12,350 --> 00:11:15,228
Oh, my gosh! It was so boring
without you at school today.

209
00:11:16,229 --> 00:11:17,939
Oh, there's an open seat.

210
00:11:18,898 --> 00:11:21,067
Okay, I'm gonna go get something to drink.

211
00:11:21,150 --> 00:11:22,151
[sighs]

212
00:11:23,945 --> 00:11:26,239
Uh, hey, sorry I took so long.

213
00:11:27,907 --> 00:11:30,743
Are you, um… Are you upset?

214
00:11:32,870 --> 00:11:34,247
Why did you bring them, too?

215
00:11:34,747 --> 00:11:37,250
Huh? Oh, well, I…

216
00:11:38,334 --> 00:11:40,169
-Ah!
-So why did Tsukasa make a call

217
00:11:40,253 --> 00:11:41,754
using your phone?

218
00:11:41,838 --> 00:11:43,631
Oh, well, he lives close.

219
00:11:43,714 --> 00:11:47,176
And he seemed like he needed help
this morning, so I let him borrow it.

220
00:11:47,260 --> 00:11:51,347
Ah, okay then. Will you tell him
to give me a call when he can?

221
00:11:51,431 --> 00:11:52,515
Um, okay.

222
00:11:52,598 --> 00:11:54,183
-[groans]
-[Rena grunts]

223
00:11:54,892 --> 00:11:56,769
Are you going to see Tsukasa after this?

224
00:11:56,853 --> 00:11:58,688
What? Um, yeah…

225
00:12:00,565 --> 00:12:04,444
-My name's Rena Kashiwagi.
-And I'm Yukika Maezono.

226
00:12:04,527 --> 00:12:06,654
[Rena] We're coming with you,
hope you don't mind.

227
00:12:06,737 --> 00:12:08,156
[stutters]

228
00:12:09,532 --> 00:12:11,159
So, that's what happened.

229
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:13,286
[sighs]

230
00:12:15,246 --> 00:12:17,999
What? Hey, where are you going?

231
00:12:22,545 --> 00:12:23,880
[Anzu exclaims]

232
00:12:26,048 --> 00:12:27,967
-[Anzu] Huh, what are you…
-Just one today?

233
00:12:28,050 --> 00:12:28,968
[Yukika] Tsukasa?

234
00:12:29,051 --> 00:12:30,386
-[Rena gasps]
-[Anzu] Uh…

235
00:12:30,470 --> 00:12:32,972
I only have plans to hang out with her.

236
00:12:33,806 --> 00:12:35,975
[Rena] What? Wait, don't go, Tsukasa!

237
00:12:36,058 --> 00:12:37,602
Huh? Um, hey…

238
00:12:38,895 --> 00:12:40,521
[breathing shakily]

239
00:12:48,112 --> 00:12:50,531
Hey, you sure? Isn't she your friend?

240
00:12:50,615 --> 00:12:54,118
Not really. She just follows me
around all the time.

241
00:12:54,619 --> 00:12:59,499
But, um, Kashiwagi, was it?
Doesn't she sort of have a thing for you?

242
00:13:01,250 --> 00:13:02,084
[Tsukasa sighs]

243
00:13:03,711 --> 00:13:05,838
-[Tsukasa] I'm so over it.
-[Anzu] What?

244
00:13:06,631 --> 00:13:09,467
I'm nice because
she's a classmate of mine,

245
00:13:09,550 --> 00:13:12,553
but I'm not interested
in dating right now.

246
00:13:15,640 --> 00:13:17,058
[Anzu] Come to think of it,

247
00:13:17,141 --> 00:13:19,143
he was pretty cold
to that other girl, too.

248
00:13:20,019 --> 00:13:23,105
Jeez, I guess hot guys
have their own issues to deal with.

249
00:13:24,190 --> 00:13:26,234
Sorry. Bringing them was wrong.

250
00:13:26,901 --> 00:13:27,818
[groans softly]

251
00:13:29,028 --> 00:13:33,574
No, they forced you to bring them.
Sorry, I was harsh.

252
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:38,621
That's okay. Yeah, it's hard
to set boundaries sometimes.

253
00:13:39,163 --> 00:13:41,082
[light music]

254
00:13:41,958 --> 00:13:43,668
-[Tsukasa] But…
-Hmm?

255
00:13:44,669 --> 00:13:47,588
You're not… you're not like them, huh?

256
00:13:48,422 --> 00:13:50,758
[Tsukasa] You didn't hound me
like everyone else does.

257
00:13:52,093 --> 00:13:54,220
So, it feels easy.

258
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:56,931
Uh…

259
00:13:58,683 --> 00:14:01,686
Well, that's good then.
[strained laugh]

260
00:14:01,769 --> 00:14:04,355
[Anzu] Well, duh, I have hostages to save.

261
00:14:05,106 --> 00:14:06,107
Oh, hey!

262
00:14:06,691 --> 00:14:10,027
Kazuki, you said you don't want
to date anyone right now, right?

263
00:14:10,111 --> 00:14:11,279
Uh, yeah.

264
00:14:11,946 --> 00:14:13,948
Well, great, 'cause me too!

265
00:14:14,031 --> 00:14:16,242
I mean there are
far more important things than that.

266
00:14:16,325 --> 00:14:17,869
[Tsukasa] Oh, uh, okay…

267
00:14:18,578 --> 00:14:20,997
[Anzu] In other words,
even if he and I become friends,

268
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:23,666
there's no chance
it will develop into a relationship.

269
00:14:23,749 --> 00:14:26,586
-That dumb devil chose the wrong cutie.
-Huh?

270
00:14:26,669 --> 00:14:28,129
[sinister laughter]

271
00:14:28,212 --> 00:14:29,714
[Tsukasa] Uh, hello?

272
00:14:30,381 --> 00:14:32,300
Oh, what'd you wanna talk about?

273
00:14:32,383 --> 00:14:34,218
[Tsukasa] Right, I-- I was wondering

274
00:14:34,302 --> 00:14:38,180
if I could temporarily
keep some of my stuff at your place?

275
00:14:38,264 --> 00:14:40,975
[Anzu] Of course.
Did you wanna bring it over now?

276
00:14:41,601 --> 00:14:43,311
I'm about to head off to work.

277
00:14:43,394 --> 00:14:45,438
But I have a realtor looking for a room.

278
00:14:45,521 --> 00:14:46,647
I see.

279
00:14:47,356 --> 00:14:49,400
[Anzu] His parents must live far away.

280
00:14:49,984 --> 00:14:52,278
Should I let him stay at my place again?

281
00:14:53,029 --> 00:14:56,532
[Anzu gasps]
That devil must've flooded Kazuki's place

282
00:14:56,616 --> 00:14:58,034
to make this whole thing happen!

283
00:14:58,534 --> 00:15:01,579
Then they kept him at my place
and broke his phone!

284
00:15:01,662 --> 00:15:03,956
It's too much drama to put on one person.

285
00:15:04,582 --> 00:15:07,376
Hey, I'll, um, reimburse you
for your phone,

286
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:09,128
but I can't do it all at once.

287
00:15:09,211 --> 00:15:11,505
I'm thinking about
getting a part-time job soon.

288
00:15:11,589 --> 00:15:12,924
-[cell phone rings]
-[both] Huh?

289
00:15:16,177 --> 00:15:17,595
Oh, good, it's the realtor.

290
00:15:18,137 --> 00:15:19,263
-I'm sorry.
-[Anzu] It's cool.

291
00:15:19,347 --> 00:15:20,222
Yes.

292
00:15:21,724 --> 00:15:22,642
Hmm.

293
00:15:27,563 --> 00:15:29,523
So, it feels easy.

294
00:15:30,858 --> 00:15:34,862
[Anzu] I thought the exact same thing
about him that night he stayed over.

295
00:15:36,697 --> 00:15:40,993
I will admit I kinda like that we feel
so comfortable around each other.

296
00:15:42,328 --> 00:15:43,496
What'd they say?

297
00:15:43,579 --> 00:15:46,165
Apparently, there aren't
any rooms available now.

298
00:15:46,248 --> 00:15:47,667
What?

299
00:15:47,750 --> 00:15:49,877
[Tsukasa] It seems
they all filled up recently.

300
00:15:49,961 --> 00:15:50,920
[growls]

301
00:15:51,003 --> 00:15:53,506
[Anzu] What if this was
that devil's handiwork, too?

302
00:15:54,090 --> 00:15:58,469
Good news is there will be one
opening up, but not for another month.

303
00:15:58,552 --> 00:16:00,012
-[Anzu groans]
-[sighs]

304
00:16:01,973 --> 00:16:03,808
[Tsukasa] You know, the cost of the phone

305
00:16:03,891 --> 00:16:06,769
is about the same price
as a month of rent.

306
00:16:06,852 --> 00:16:08,062
[groans]

307
00:16:08,145 --> 00:16:09,772
[Tsukasa] Hey, if it's cool with you…

308
00:16:09,855 --> 00:16:10,773
Huh?

309
00:16:11,816 --> 00:16:15,987
How about for a month, I stay
at your place and we call it even.

310
00:16:18,739 --> 00:16:20,032
[gasps]

311
00:16:20,116 --> 00:16:23,786
-What?
-[evil laughter]

312
00:16:24,495 --> 00:16:28,124
Huh? Stay at my place for a month?

313
00:16:28,874 --> 00:16:31,752
I'm not asking you
to let me stay there for nothing.

314
00:16:32,378 --> 00:16:34,672
I'll help out with the chores, of course.

315
00:16:34,755 --> 00:16:35,798
Chores?

316
00:16:36,590 --> 00:16:40,678
[Tsukasa] When I don't have work,
I'll make dinner and the next day's lunch.

317
00:16:40,761 --> 00:16:41,887
[Anzu] Uh, oh…

318
00:16:42,388 --> 00:16:45,182
And if "that thing" comes back,
I'll get rid of it.

319
00:16:45,266 --> 00:16:47,601
[narrator] Roaches are unseemly,
so instead, cake.

320
00:16:47,685 --> 00:16:49,186
And as for me,

321
00:16:49,270 --> 00:16:52,189
it's close to where I work,
so it'll be a huge help.

322
00:16:53,315 --> 00:16:54,984
[Anzu] What should I do?

323
00:16:55,067 --> 00:16:57,486
His conditions
are too delicious to pass up!

324
00:16:57,570 --> 00:17:01,115
Uh, but still,
knowing that stinking devil…

325
00:17:01,699 --> 00:17:04,076
-Ouch!
-Um, let me see that.

326
00:17:04,702 --> 00:17:06,120
-[gasps]
-[smooching]

327
00:17:06,203 --> 00:17:08,873
[Anzu] He'll just set up
insanely cheesy situations over and over.

328
00:17:08,956 --> 00:17:11,584
-[screams]
-Oh, sorry!

329
00:17:11,667 --> 00:17:13,294
I didn't mean to, hon.

330
00:17:14,462 --> 00:17:15,629
[exclaims]

331
00:17:15,713 --> 00:17:18,716
[Anzu] That must be
their entire intention!

332
00:17:21,886 --> 00:17:22,887
[boy moans]

333
00:17:22,970 --> 00:17:24,889
[giggles]

334
00:17:24,972 --> 00:17:25,973
[grunts]

335
00:17:26,057 --> 00:17:29,143
My bad, um,
it's a crazy favor to ask of you.

336
00:17:29,226 --> 00:17:30,811
[Anzu] No, no, Not at all.

337
00:17:30,895 --> 00:17:33,981
If you're okay with it,
I don't mind having you stay at my place.

338
00:17:34,774 --> 00:17:36,150
That would be great.

339
00:17:36,734 --> 00:17:37,735
[laughing awkwardly]

340
00:17:37,818 --> 00:17:41,655
[Anzu] Shoot! I responded impulsively
out of this sense of guilt.

341
00:17:42,531 --> 00:17:45,534
[Tsukasa] Would you explain it all
to your parents, too?

342
00:17:46,035 --> 00:17:47,870
[sighs]
No worries there.

343
00:17:47,953 --> 00:17:50,081
They won't have any issues with it.

344
00:17:50,164 --> 00:17:52,666
[both] Sure, it's fine by me!

345
00:17:53,667 --> 00:17:56,420
-[meowing]
-[phone buzzing]

346
00:17:56,504 --> 00:17:58,047
[Anzu moans]

347
00:18:01,383 --> 00:18:03,177
[meowing continues]

348
00:18:04,512 --> 00:18:06,138
[grunts]
That dream.

349
00:18:07,014 --> 00:18:10,726
Even I think it was pretty pathetic.
What a crazy dream.

350
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:13,437
Me living with a hot guy.

351
00:18:13,521 --> 00:18:15,523
[bright music]

352
00:18:16,941 --> 00:18:18,275
You're finally awake.

353
00:18:18,776 --> 00:18:22,321
[Anzu] It wasn't a dream.
It's all coming back to me now.

354
00:18:22,404 --> 00:18:23,697
Oh, wow, good morning.

355
00:18:23,781 --> 00:18:26,575
Morning. You've got an early bed hair.

356
00:18:26,659 --> 00:18:29,328
Yay! You're actually
making my lunch for me.

357
00:18:29,411 --> 00:18:31,247
[Tsukasa] Well, that was part of the deal.

358
00:18:34,291 --> 00:18:35,334
[sighs]

359
00:18:36,502 --> 00:18:40,798
[Anzu] Amazing. I get to wake up
to a cutie making lunch in my kitchen.

360
00:18:42,091 --> 00:18:45,427
Seriously, hot guys are hot
no matter what they do.

361
00:18:46,887 --> 00:18:49,181
Kazuki, you're an early bird, huh.

362
00:18:49,265 --> 00:18:50,891
You just wake up late.

363
00:18:50,975 --> 00:18:52,101
Yeah.

364
00:18:52,184 --> 00:18:56,313
[Anzu] Now that I think about it,
he did seem to be really tired yesterday.

365
00:18:56,397 --> 00:18:58,065
-[Anzu] Long day?
-[Tsukasa] Yeah.

366
00:18:59,775 --> 00:19:01,902
I'm gonna take a bath and crash.

367
00:19:02,653 --> 00:19:05,531
[Anzu] First, he cleaned up
his totally flooded place,

368
00:19:06,157 --> 00:19:09,076
and then he did
like a million loads of laundry,

369
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:11,203
and he had to be at work late.

370
00:19:12,079 --> 00:19:16,041
And after all that, he's still up
making us lunch this morning.

371
00:19:17,668 --> 00:19:20,087
-[Tsukasa] Hoshino, do you eat breakfast?
-Hm.

372
00:19:20,671 --> 00:19:21,797
Yes, I do!

373
00:19:21,881 --> 00:19:24,091
All right, then I'll make something quick.

374
00:19:24,175 --> 00:19:25,384
[Anzu exclaims]

375
00:19:26,427 --> 00:19:28,345
[Anzu] Thanks, Mom.

376
00:19:28,429 --> 00:19:29,346
[Tsukasa] Yeah, yeah.

377
00:19:30,931 --> 00:19:33,350
WEATHER FORECAST

378
00:19:34,059 --> 00:19:34,935
[Tsukasa] Here you go.

379
00:19:35,019 --> 00:19:36,854
Yay!
[chuckles]

380
00:19:36,937 --> 00:19:38,063
Time to eat!

381
00:19:38,564 --> 00:19:40,733
Ha, um!
[munches]

382
00:19:40,816 --> 00:19:42,359
[delighted moan]

383
00:19:42,443 --> 00:19:44,236
Oh, I need gym clothes.

384
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:47,281
-[Anzu] Um, they were still drying.
-I'll go get them.

385
00:19:47,364 --> 00:19:50,868
-Um, can you pack my lunch for me?
-[Anzu] Yeah.

386
00:19:51,619 --> 00:19:54,622
[Anzu] I don't have to make lunch
or even breakfast.

387
00:19:54,705 --> 00:19:56,957
And he is a feast for the eyes.

388
00:19:57,041 --> 00:19:59,376
This might be a great situation after all.

389
00:20:00,336 --> 00:20:02,755
And I haven't seen
that devil around either.

390
00:20:02,838 --> 00:20:04,298
Good morning!

391
00:20:04,381 --> 00:20:06,508
-Ugh, speak of the devil!
-Oh, jeez.

392
00:20:06,592 --> 00:20:07,426
[giggles]

393
00:20:07,509 --> 00:20:11,931
Have you been enjoying
your oh-so-romantic dating-sim scenarios?

394
00:20:12,014 --> 00:20:14,683
Why don't you shut up?
You put Kazuki through too much!

395
00:20:14,767 --> 00:20:16,393
Be more considerate!

396
00:20:16,977 --> 00:20:19,063
Yeah, yeah, you say that,

397
00:20:19,146 --> 00:20:22,900
but you've been stuffing your face
with breakfast like a hamster.

398
00:20:22,983 --> 00:20:24,652
-[Anzu] Shut up!
-[munching]

399
00:20:24,735 --> 00:20:26,320
And just so you know,

400
00:20:26,403 --> 00:20:29,365
Kazuki isn't interested
in dating anyone right now.

401
00:20:29,448 --> 00:20:32,826
Too bad! You chose the wrong guy!
You're a big stupid dummy.

402
00:20:32,910 --> 00:20:34,912
[humming mockingly]

403
00:20:36,705 --> 00:20:38,749
-[grunts]
-You're the stupid one, Anzu!

404
00:20:38,832 --> 00:20:42,711
Romance is unpredictable
because people always change their minds.

405
00:20:43,212 --> 00:20:47,132
And plus, did you forget what I told you?

406
00:20:47,800 --> 00:20:50,636
You're about to live
a dating sim-lifestyle

407
00:20:50,719 --> 00:20:52,763
surrounded by hotties…

408
00:20:52,846 --> 00:20:54,974
-Oh, watch your step!
-[giggles]

409
00:20:55,057 --> 00:20:56,892
…in real life.

410
00:20:56,976 --> 00:20:59,520
-[both grunt]
-[doorbell dings]

411
00:20:59,603 --> 00:21:00,854
-Huh?
-Hm?

412
00:21:01,438 --> 00:21:03,857
-Who's here so early?
-Ooh…

413
00:21:03,941 --> 00:21:05,859
-Be right there.
-[chuckles]

414
00:21:06,527 --> 00:21:09,571
[Anzu] Hm? Our school uniform? Who is it?

415
00:21:10,239 --> 00:21:12,449
I'm not done, so don't disappear!

416
00:21:12,533 --> 00:21:15,160
-I still have a lot to say.
-[Riri] Sure, sure!

417
00:21:15,244 --> 00:21:16,245
[Anzu] Coming.

418
00:21:18,831 --> 00:21:20,416
-Huh?
-[Junta] Morning.

419
00:21:20,499 --> 00:21:22,501
[bright music]

420
00:21:25,754 --> 00:21:27,006
How did you sleep, Anzu?

421
00:21:27,506 --> 00:21:28,882
[giggles nervously]

422
00:21:30,426 --> 00:21:32,928
Did you wake up late? Time for school.

423
00:21:34,805 --> 00:21:37,308
[Anzu] Who is this tall drink of water?

424
00:21:37,933 --> 00:21:39,268
Um… Uh…

425
00:21:40,936 --> 00:21:43,689
-Have we met somewhere before?
-[Junta] What?

426
00:21:44,356 --> 00:21:45,691
[Junta laughs]

427
00:21:45,774 --> 00:21:48,277
Wait, what are you saying?
You still asleep?

428
00:21:49,570 --> 00:21:52,531
Don't tell me you forgot your old friend.

429
00:21:53,782 --> 00:21:55,451
[Anzu] My old friend?

430
00:21:55,534 --> 00:21:57,202
[Tsukasa] Hoshino, what are you doing?

431
00:21:58,287 --> 00:22:00,039
You should get going.

432
00:22:02,791 --> 00:22:03,625
Huh?

433
00:22:05,294 --> 00:22:06,170
Uh.

434
00:22:06,795 --> 00:22:08,047
[Anzu gasps]

435
00:22:08,839 --> 00:22:11,717
[Anzu] Dearest Mom and Dad,

436
00:22:12,676 --> 00:22:15,179
how's life in the United States going?

437
00:22:16,305 --> 00:22:19,058
I've been forced
to live a sad and lonely life

438
00:22:19,141 --> 00:22:21,310
without my three greatest desires.

439
00:22:22,019 --> 00:22:27,149
But then a super hot guy became
my roommate which feels majorly awkward.

440
00:22:29,818 --> 00:22:33,614
Next, a childhood friend
who I know absolutely nothing about

441
00:22:33,697 --> 00:22:35,157
suddenly appeared.

442
00:22:35,824 --> 00:22:39,745
And now, everything is about
to get awfully complicated.

443
00:22:42,873 --> 00:22:44,374
A fanfare, please!

444
00:22:44,458 --> 00:22:46,502
And a big congratulations!

445
00:22:46,585 --> 00:22:48,754
Did you fall for my little trick?

446
00:22:48,837 --> 00:22:52,007
I bet now you don't feel like
skipping the ending, right?

447
00:22:52,091 --> 00:22:55,552
In today's world, you can watch
whatever you want at your own convenience.

448
00:22:55,636 --> 00:22:58,430
But don't you think in that process
we've also lost something?

449
00:22:58,514 --> 00:23:00,808
[sighs]
Don't just let things be! Come on!

450
00:23:00,891 --> 00:23:03,477
Let's go on a super-duper happy adventure!

451
00:23:03,560 --> 00:23:05,479
So I can make sure I get paid.

452
00:23:05,562 --> 00:23:07,731
[closing theme music]

453
00:23:07,815 --> 00:23:08,649
♪ Ah, yeah! ♪

454
00:23:11,276 --> 00:23:12,111
♪ Let's go! ♪

455
00:23:14,530 --> 00:23:15,614
♪ Lo-love! ♪

456
00:23:17,866 --> 00:23:18,700
♪ Here we go! ♪

457
00:00:01,641 --> 00:00:05,102
In today's world, you can watch
